# Not committed deliberately: Tailwind v4's lightningcss (and a few other deps) ship
# platform-specific native binaries as optionalDependencies. A lockfile generated on one OS
# only resolves that OS's binary, so `npm install` on a different platform (dev on Windows,
# deployed on Vercel's Linux) fails to find the right one. Letting each environment generate
# its own lockfile via a plain `npm install` sidesteps that entirely.
package-lock.json
frontend/package-lock.json
backend/package-lock.json

.env
.env.local
*.env
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
*.log

